From: McKernel Rust Migration <mckernel@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] objtool: recognize Rust 1.92 Vec swap_remove panic
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 02:00:00 +0000

Rocky-Base: linux-6.12.0-211.44.1.el10_2
Observed-Rustc: 1.92.0
License: GPL-2.0-only

Native zeroing releases retained ledger entries with Vec::swap_remove. Rust
1.92 emits its out-of-bounds call to a nested assert_failed function with
return type !. The exact compiler library source and alloc.o confirm that
this function panics rather than returning. Its two call sites in the native
module are incorrectly reported as falling through to the next function.

Extend the existing Rust noreturn classifier with only the observed mangled
path suffix, alongside Vec::remove. Keep all control-flow and stack checks,
including rejection of unknown callees. This is a project-observed compiler
compatibility adjustment; no upstream or stable commit is claimed.

Signed-off-by: McKernel Rust Migration <mckernel@localhost>
---
 tools/objtool/check.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/tools/objtool/check.c b/tools/objtool/check.c
--- a/tools/objtool/check.c
+++ b/tools/objtool/check.c
@@ -207,6 +207,7 @@ static bool is_rust_noreturn(const struct symbol *func)
 	return str_ends_with(func->name, "_4core5sliceSp15copy_from_slice17len_mismatch_fail")		||
 	       str_ends_with(func->name, "_4core5slice4sort6shared9smallsort22panic_on_ord_violation")	||
 	       str_ends_with(func->name, "_5alloc3vecINtB6_3VecppE6remove13assert_failed")		||
+	       str_ends_with(func->name, "_5alloc3vecINtB6_3VecppE11swap_remove13assert_failed")	||
 	       str_ends_with(func->name, "_4core6option13unwrap_failed")				||
 	       str_ends_with(func->name, "_4core6result13unwrap_failed")				||
 	       str_ends_with(func->name, "_4core9panicking5panic")					||
